DOES A SLOPPY POOL MAKE A BAD SIGNAL
9116 A/B signals, 103 symbols, 333 days, Min30. cap under test: 0.2 ATR (the reference's).

  pool width in ATR:  p50 0.123   p75 0.216   p90 0.319   p95 0.400   p99 0.560
  2672 of 9116 signals (29%) come from a pool wider than the reference would allow.

========================================================================================================
EARLY SIGNALS — the arm the observation is about
========================================================================================================
                                               R/sig      n       R/sig      n
  pool < 0.2 ATR (ref cap)  vs  >= 0.2        +0.000   5549  vs  +0.028   2160   diff -0.028  |z|  0.9

  by width band, each against everything else:
    0.00 - 0.05 ATR                           +0.023   2530  vs  +0.001   5179   diff +0.023  |z|  0.8
    0.05 - 0.20 ATR                           -0.019   3019  vs  +0.026   4690   diff -0.045  |z|  1.6
    0.20 - 0.40 ATR                           +0.024   1803  vs  +0.003   5906   diff +0.021  |z|  0.6
    0.40 - 9.90 ATR                           +0.049    357  vs  +0.006   7352   diff +0.043  |z|  0.6

