========================================================================================================
BOTH HALVES OF THE WINDOW — early stream
========================================================================================================
    half 1: pool < 0.2 vs >=                  +0.004   2721  vs  +0.038   1124   diff -0.034  |z|  0.8
    half 2: pool < 0.2 vs >=                  -0.003   2828  vs  +0.018   1036   diff -0.021  |z|  0.5

  an effect in one half only is a non-result. that is the bar
  twenty-one entry filters failed.

========================================================================================================
THE STOP-SIZE CONTROL — is width just the fee denominator?
========================================================================================================
  stop terciles at 1.05% and 1.80% of price
    tight stops: pool < 0.2 vs >=             -0.017   1398  vs  +0.018    626   diff -0.035  |z|  0.5
    mid stops: pool < 0.2 vs >=               +0.042   1465  vs  +0.067    559   diff -0.025  |z|  0.4
    wide stops: pool < 0.2 vs >=              -0.025   1490  vs  +0.023    535   diff -0.048  |z|  0.7

  the width effect must hold INSIDE each tercile. if it only
  appears across them, it is the fee denominator wearing a costume.

========================================================================================================
THE STAIRCASE TEST — does width hurt most AGAINST the trend?
========================================================================================================
    signal AGREES with HTF trend              +0.000   5549  vs  +0.028   2160   diff -0.028  |z|  0.9
    signal FIGHTS the HTF trend              too few  (0 / 0)

  the mechanism predicts a BIGGER gap on the fighting row. equal
  gaps mean width matters but the staircase story does not.

========================================================================================================
WHAT IT WOULD COST — capping the pool at 0.2 ATR
========================================================================================================
  early       keeps  5549 of  7709 (72%)   R/sig +0.008 -> +0.000   total    +63.7 ->     +2.2
  confirmed   keeps   895 of  1407 (64%)   R/sig +0.018 -> +0.042   total    +25.7 ->    +37.9

  a filter that raises R per signal while cutting total R is
  deleting winners. read both columns, never just the first.
